;;; core.category -- finite category theory as one library: the shared base
;;; layer for computations with categories, functors, (co)limits, Kan
;;; extensions, adjunctions and monads, built on the finite-category
;;; representation of core.sheaf.site.
;;;
;;; Usage: (require core.category)
;;;
;;; Loads the whole facility (each part can also be required alone):
;;;   core.sheaf.site          the representation: finite categories, sieves,
;;;                            sites (ADR-0033); re-used, never re-encoded
;;;   core.sheaf.presheaf      presheaves of sets, matching families, plus
;;;   core.category.finite     standard shapes, presentations, monoids and
;;;                            groups, products, coproducts, full
;;;                            subcategories, the nerve and its cohomology
;;;   core.category.functor    functors, natural transformations, functor
;;;                            categories, comma and slice categories, the
;;;                            Grothendieck construction, adjunctions, monads
;;;   core.category.set        Set-valued functors: limits, colimits, ends,
;;;                            coends, Yoneda, categories of elements
;;;   core.category.kan        Kan extensions by the pointwise and the (co)end
;;;                            formulas, Lan -| F^* -| Ran, descent as a right
;;;                            Kan extension on thin sites
;;;   core.category.linear     limits, colimits and derived limits of diagrams
;;;                            of free Z-modules and Q-vector spaces
;;;   core.category.descent    the sheaf condition as a limit over sieve
;;;                            categories, the Cech equalizer, sheafification
;;;                            as the reflector a -| i and its monad
;;;   core.category.cohomology abelian descent: Cech cohomology and
;;;                            cohomological descent as derived limits over
;;;                            nerve categories and Grothendieck constructions
;;;
;;; Reference: docs/reference/stdlib/category.md; design: ADR-0036
;;; (docs/design/adr/0036-core-category-finite-categories.md).
;;; Sources: S. Mac Lane, "Categories for the Working Mathematician" (1998);
;;; E. Riehl, "Category Theory in Context" (2016); G. M. Kelly, "Basic
;;; Concepts of Enriched Category Theory" (1982); S. Mac Lane, I. Moerdijk,
;;; "Sheaves in Geometry and Logic" (1992).

(require core.sheaf.site)
(require core.sheaf.presheaf)
(require core.category.finite)
(require core.category.functor)
(require core.category.set)
(require core.category.kan)
(require core.category.linear)
(require core.category.descent)
(require core.category.cohomology)
